``` SR-03 | Scheduler Hitting Its Concurrency Limit
    Splunk Administrator Field Manual - Gaurav Malik

    Use case: Skips are climbing and the scheduler appears saturated; measure
    actual concurrent scheduled-search load against the limit and find the
    long-running searches holding the slots.
    Run on: SH. In an SHC, run against all members; each member enforces its
    own limit.
    Query: Slot hogs over the same window (SH)
    If this returns nothing, run probes/SR-03-probe.spl to confirm the data it
    reads exists here.
```
index=_internal sourcetype=scheduler status=success earliest=-24h
| stats count as runs sum(run_time) as total_runtime_s
        median(run_time) as median_runtime_s max(run_time) as max_runtime_s
        by app savedsearch_name user
| eval slot_hours=round(total_runtime_s / 3600, 2)
| sort - slot_hours
| head 20
